+  // Like flushPool(), dump the pending constant pool entries (if any), but
+  // only emit veneers for short-range branches that would expire within the
+  // ShortRangeBranchHysteresis window. flushPool() passes SIZE_MAX, which
+  // turns *every* pending short-range branch into a branch-to-veneer; this
+  // variant keeps branches that are not about to expire short.
+  //
+  // After this returns (and absent OOM) the constant pool is empty and no
+  // registered short-range branch expires within ShortRangeBranchHysteresis
+  // bytes, so the next few plain instructions are emitted without an
